GRAFT builds on the following work. It does not copy their code; it uses GOAt and MemoryAgentBench as
git submodules pointing at their own repositories, which keep their own terms (at the time of writing the
GOAt and EiG-Search repositories carry no license file).

- GOAt: Shengyao Lu, Keith G. Mills, Jiao He, Bang Liu, Di Niu. "GOAt: Explaining Graph Neural Networks via
  Graph Output Attribution." ICLR 2024. https://github.com/sluxsr/GOAt (submodule my_method/gnn/GOAt)
- EiG-Search: Shengyao Lu, Bang Liu, Keith G. Mills, Jiao He, Di Niu. "EiG-Search: Generating Edge-Induced
  Subgraphs for GNN Explanation in Linear Time." ICML 2024. https://github.com/sluxsr/EiG-Search
  (GRAFT's my_method/gnn/eig.py is an independent batched implementation of the EiG-Search edge scoring)
- MemoryAgentBench (FactConsolidation data and baselines): https://github.com/HUST-AI-HYZ/MemoryAgentBench
  (submodule baselines/memoryagentbench)
